edbi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fredbi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fredbi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fredbi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fredbi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2020-05-28T16:49:07Z","updated_at":"2020-11-15T20:22:09Z","closed_at":"2020-11-15T20:22:09Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm not sure if this a problem or a question...I read through a few discussions on nullable vs required in the issue log. I didn't read them all in-depth, but the ones I did, did not directly state a workaround for my case. Sorry if this is a repeat, I know the topic is trying. \r\n\r\n## Problem statement\r\nIt doesn't seem possible to have a `map[string]interface{}` dictionary property be 1) required (i.e. the field is provided in the content body) and 2) the field is validated as a non-nil value.\r\n\r\nThe spec below makes sure the field `data` is in the content payload, but it doesn't seem to care if it is `null` (for JSON) and maps to Go's `nil`.\r\n\r\n## Swagger specification\r\nSee the `data` property below.\r\n```\r\n  configCreate:\r\n    type: object\r\n    required:\r\n      - name\r\n      - type\r\n      - data\r\n    properties:\r\n      tags:\r\n        $ref: '#/definitions/tags'\r\n      name:\r\n        type: string\r\n      type:\r\n        type: string\r\n      data:\r\n        type: object\r\n        x-nullable: false\r\n        additionalProperties:\r\n          type: object\r\n```\r\nI tried throwing `x-nullable: false` in which doesn't appear to work. I can always add my own logic, but before I do I want to make sure there is isn't something in-spec that I can do.\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\nswagger version: dev, built from master, c1166eb2\r\ngo version: 1.14.3\r\nOS:   Windows 10\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"casualjim","id":456109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjEwOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/456109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim","html_url":"https://github.com/casualjim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/casualjim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-swagger/go-swagger/issues/2300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-swagger/go-swagger/issues/2300/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}